  "notes": "CONJUGATION (ichidan):\n- Negative: ぶら{下|さ}げない\n- Te-form: ぶら{下|さ}げて\n- Past: ぶら{下|さ}げた\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive. The intransitive counterpart is ぶら{下|さ}がる (to hang down, to dangle).\n\nUSAGE:\nImplies a casual or loose way of carrying or hanging something. Often suggests the object swings or sways.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {首|くび}からぶら{下|さ}げる: to hang from the neck\n- {手|て}にぶら{下|さ}げる: to dangle from the hand\n- {天井|てんじょう}からぶら{下|さ}げる: to hang from the ceiling",
